### Addendum after merging master (branch head bdf1c26)

Mechanism (4) is now FIXED for the two members observed failing that way.
`_assert_fd_released` (tests/test_tts_interrupt.py) compares the
`(st_dev, st_ino)` captured when the descriptor was created, so "closed" and
"already handed to someone else" both count as released. Deterministic
before/after, no load:

    nothing reopens                      old=pass                        new=pass
    number reclaimed by unrelated open   old=FAIL: DID NOT RAISE OSError new=pass

Applied at test_pipe_creation_publishes_both_fds_before_delivered_sigint and
test_outer_pidfd_is_owned_before_delivered_sigint. NINE further
`pytest.raises(OSError)` + `errno.EBADF` sites in the same file carry the same
latent race and want the same treatment: lines 4002, 4052, 4072, 4097, 4198,
4324, 4560, 4787, 7917 (pre-merge numbering). Not touched, because none was
observed failing and a blind sweep should not land unverified.

Worth stating because it changes how this bug should be read: mechanisms (1)
and (4) are NOT load-dependent at all. (1) depends on how the suite was
launched and on file ordering; (4) depends only on whether anything else in the
process happened to open a file between the close and the assertion. That is a
better explanation for **disjoint failure sets across consecutive identical
runs** than CPU contention is, and it is why the family looked load-driven
without being so.

Coverage of the newer candidates:
- test_pre_submit_interrupt_does_not_strand_false_running_state: FIXED,
  mechanism (3), was one of the `-2` returncodes.
- test_pipe_creation_publishes_both_fds_before_delivered_sigint: FIXED,
  mechanism (4).
- test_cli_pending_sigint_during_boundary_install_is_typed_and_traceback_free:
  defect class addressed (budgets + disposition); never observed failing here,
  so not claimed as verified.
- tests/test_ask_capture_deadline.py: NOT covered. Out of the two files I
  touched. It has the same fixed-budget shape (`released.wait(timeout=2.0)`
